<item>
            <title>[PARQUET-227] Parquet thrift can write unions that have 0 or more than 1 set value</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PARQUET-227</link>
                <project id="12315521" key="PARQUET">Parquet</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Having 0 or more than 1 set values means the data will be unreadable in the read path, this should not be allowed in the write path.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="12785445">PARQUET-227</key>
            <summary>Parquet thrift can write unions that have 0 or more than 1 set value</summary>
