                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="14380673" author="rdblue" created="Wed, 25 Mar 2015 20:17:48 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Should we define a type annotation for unions? That way Avro, Thrift, and Hive unions could be compatible. That would also be a good opportunity to standardize behavior, so if a union has multiple non-null values we have predictable behavior for interpreting the data across object models. Obviously, this wouldn&apos;t block your work here.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14380779" author="alexlevenson" created="Wed, 25 Mar 2015 21:09:40 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Yeah that makes sense to me.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14520945" author="alexlevenson" created="Thu, 30 Apr 2015 06:19:06 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Issue resolved by pull request 153&lt;br/&gt;
